<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
Audit H12.1 — `darpan.reconciliation.NsAuthConfig` and `darpan.reconciliation.NsRestletConfig` were
previously declared in BOTH this file AND `darpan/entity/ReconciliationEntities.xml`. Whichever
component loaded last silently overwrote the other's definition, and field-set drift between the
two copies would be undetectable. The canonical definitions live in the `darpan` component (the
DARPAN_ACTIVE_COMPANY_SCOPE EntityFilter set in darpan/data/SecuritySeedData.xml already references
them there). This component is the consumer, not the owner — the netsuite-darpan scripts continue
to `ec.entity.find('darpan.reconciliation.NsAuthConfig'/...)` and resolve to the canonical entity.

This file is intentionally empty (just the entities root element) so the entity-loader scan does not
trip on a missing file in a directory it expects to enumerate.
-->
<entities xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="http://moqui.org/xsd/entity-definition-3.xsd">
</entities>
